2026-11-08 Fix requested for cargo test --all-features --all-targets --workspace failing at custom offline benchmark.
Reproduction: cargo test -p rocketmq-classic --bench offline --locked --offline -v => panic at release-only assertion. Verbose Cargo invocation shows a harness=false executable built with cfg(test), invoked without arguments. cfg(test) cannot distinguish Cargo bench from test, nor can debug_assertions distinguish release-profile tests from measurements.
Fix: main checks Cargo's --bench argument before starting measurements. Without the marker it reports skipped measurement and exits successfully; with the marker the existing release-only assertion and complete benchmark body remain intact. No changes to measured inputs/loops, allocation tracking, iterations or published APIs. Added execution guidance in docs/testing/cleanup-validation.md.
Targeted debug cargo test --bench offline --all-features --locked --offline: PASS, explicit skip message. Direct debug executable with --bench: expected release assertion confirmed (not a pass for measurements). Strict facade all-target/all-feature Clippy, formatting and diff checks: PASS. Full all-target workspace tests and real release benchmark validation running at this entry.
Release measurement validation: cargo bench -p rocketmq-classic --bench offline --locked --offline -v => PASS; Cargo invoked the executable with --bench and all five timing/allocation measurement groups ran. No timing/performance comparison is claimed.
Release test-mode validation: cargo test --release -p rocketmq-classic --bench offline --all-features --locked --offline => PASS with explicit skip message, confirming release-profile tests do not trigger measurement. Debug direct --bench invocation retains the original panic as expected. Only argument dispatch/documentation changed; no dependencies or lockfiles touched.
2026-11-09 Final verification: cargo test --all-features --all-targets --workspace --locked --offline => PASS, 1816 tests across 92 test harnesses; offline custom benchmark explicitly skipped measurements. Formal cargo bench still completed all five measurement groups. Formatting, strict affected-crate Clippy and diff checks passed. All requested automatic work complete.
